  "gaps": [
    "Listed blocks sum to 123 credits (33 GCF + 57 major + 33 electives) against a 120-credit total; the capture says 3 major credits (ECO 203, marked *) also satisfy Global Campus Foundations requirements, but does not state which specific Foundations course or requirement ECO 203 replaces, so the overlap cannot be removed from a specific line.",
    "The Global Campus Foundations courses are taken from the standard sequence; the capture says courses may be substituted, and no program-specific Foundations list is printed for this major.",
    "Credits for TEC 100 Computer Literacy are not printed; 3 credits assumed because it replaces GEN 102 (3 credits) in the sequence for this program (listed as 'Bachelor of Science in Cyber Data Security Technology').",
    "GEN 101 Developing Skills and Strategies for Success (3 credits) is scheduled as the first course and satisfies 3 elective credits; GEN 104 also satisfies 3 elective credits for students transferring fewer than 30 credits. How much of the 33-credit elective block remains open is not itemized.",
    "The credit unit is printed only as 'credits'; semester credits are assumed but not explicitly stated in the capture.",
    "Residency requirement: a minimum of 30 credits must be completed at the University, but no specific courses are designated as institution-only.",
    "Upper-division requirement: minimum of 30 upper-division credits, including 18 in the major; which elective credits must be upper-division is not specified.",
    "CYB 300 lists prerequisite INT 301, which does not appear in the program requirements; how it is satisfied is not stated.",
    "ENG 328 requires fulfillment of the 'Natural Scientist Perspective requirement', which is not defined in the capture.",
    "Students must complete MAT 222 and MAT 233 (or transfer equivalents); CYB 499 must be taken last in the program.",
    "Minimum cumulative GPA of 2.00 in all coursework attempted at the University is required for graduation."
  ],
